SIMP={2015:[["FIFA corruption investigation","The 2014 episode 'You Don't Have to Live Like a Referee' did satirise World Cup referee bribery. It drew attention after the 2015 FIFA investigation."]],
2016:[["Trump elected president","The 2000 episode 'Bart to the Future' really has a 'after President Trump' line. But the comparison clip that spread with it was a promo made in July 2015, after he announced his run."]],
2017:[["Trump touching a glowing orb","A parody posted on the official Facebook page five days after the real event (21 May). Not from an episode."]],
2018:[["Canada legalises recreational cannabis","The 2005 'Midnight Rx' scene is real. The topic was already being debated in Canada at the time."],["US men win Olympic curling gold","The 2010 'Boy Meets Curl' scene is real. Seen as coincidence."]],
2019:[["Disney completes its purchase of 21st Century Fox","The 1998 sign gag 'A Division of Walt Disney Co' is real. A joke that came true."],["Notre-Dame fire","The cathedral in the 2007 episode does not catch fire. The flames and Mr Burns were edited in."],["Trump's idea of buying Greenland","No such episode exists."]],
2020:[["COVID-19","The word 'coronavirus' was edited into the 'Osaka flu' scene of the 1993 episode 'Marge in Chains'."],["George Floyd's death","A painting by the artist Yuri Pomo made after the event. Not from an episode."],["Beirut port explosion","Explosion scenes from two different episodes stitched together."]],
2021:[["Storming of the US Capitol","No evidence for the claimed link to a 1996 episode."],["The film 'The Matrix 4'","A 2004 line joking about a fourth film is real."]],
2022:[["Russia's invasion of Ukraine","A collage of images from a 2019 episode, a 2016 mobile game and a 2010 episode. No mention of Ukraine or 2022."]],
2023:[["Collapse of Silicon Valley Bank","A doctored clip of a 1995 scene with the bank's name changed to 'Silicon Valley Bank'. Originally the First Bank of Springfield."],["Loss of the Titan submersible","Only vaguely similar to a 2006 episode. Seen as coincidence."],["Trump indicted and arrested","No supporting scene has been found."]],
2024:[["Cypress Hill with the London Symphony Orchestra","The 1996 'Homerpalooza' gag is real. It came true with a 2024 concert at the Royal Albert Hall."]],
2025:[["The 'Simpsons predictions for this year' lists that circulate every January","Most images show no source scene. Only verified cases will be added."]],
2026:[["Claims that went viral this year","Being checked. Only verified cases will be added at year end."]]}
EXTRA_SIMP='<h3 class="sh" style="margin-top:40px">Other \'they predicted it\' claims that keep circulating</h3><p style="color:var(--muted)">Claims about events before 2015, or with no year.</p><div class="cl" style="margin-top:12px"><div class="claim mid"><div class="h"><b>Super Bowl winner (1992)</b><span class="b mid">@MID@</span></div><p>The Washington win in the 1992 episode \'Lisa the Greek\' is real. A version with the names changed for a 1993 rerun also circulated, adding to the confusion.</p><p class="src">@SRC@<a href="https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/The_Simpsons_future_predictions" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Wikipedia summary</a></p></div><div class="claim no"><div class="h"><b>Ebola outbreak (2014)</b><span class="b no">@NO@</span></div><p>A book-title gag in the 1997 episode \'Lisa\'s Sax\'. Ebola had been known since 1976 and a major outbreak had already happened in 1995.</p><p class="src">@SRC@<a href="https://leadstories.com/hoax-alert/2021/05/fact-check-the-simpsons-did-not-predict-george-floyd-death-the-notre-dame-fire-the-ebola-breakout-or-donald-trump-touching-an-orb.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Lead Stories</a></p></div><div class="claim no"><div class="h"><b>Autocorrect</b><span class="b no">@NO@</span></div><p>The 1994 scene is real, but word-processor autocorrect and handwriting-recognition devices (1993) already existed.</p><p class="src">@SRC@<a href="https://www.snopes.com/list/simpson-predictions-internet-hoaxes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Snopes</a></p></div><div class="claim mid"><div class="h"><b>Smartwatch</b><span class="b mid">@MID@</span></div><p>The 1995 scene is real, but wrist communicators had been a common idea in comics since the 1940s.</p><p class="src">@SRC@<a href="https://www.snopes.com/list/simpson-predictions-internet-hoaxes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Snopes</a></p></div><div class="claim no"><div class="h"><b>Censorship row over Michelangelo\'s David</b><span class="b no">@NO@</span></div><p>The 1990 scene satirised a censorship debate that dates back to 1504.</p><p class="src">@SRC@<a href="https://www.snopes.com/list/simpson-predictions-internet-hoaxes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Snopes</a></p></div></div>'
